      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>The Ramp &amp; Tail‑Lift Loading stage is the pivotal moment when a bike parcel transitions from carrier to transport vehicle, and it hinges on three disciplined steps: positioning, hydraulic operation, and secure placement. Mastery of each step guarantees a zero‑scratch journey, whether the parcel rides on a city bus or travels the rails.</p>

<h3>Positioning</h3>
<p>Operators first align the bike parcel’s frame with the ramp’s guide rails. Precise lateral placement ensures the tail‑lift’s fork engages the bike’s rear axle without contact to the handlebars or pedals.</p>
<p>Laser‑assisted markers on modern ramps provide visual cues, allowing the crew to center the parcel within a 2‑centimeter tolerance. This exactness is critical because any misalignment can amplify forces during the lift, risking cosmetic damage.</p>

<h3>Hydraulic Operation</h3>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Once positioned, the hydraulic tail‑lift raises the bike in a smooth, controlled arc.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Pressure sensors monitor the lift’s force, automatically adjusting flow to stay below the 150 N threshold set by the zero‑scratch policy.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The hydraulic system’s low‑vibration design reduces shock, and a built‑in lock‑out prevents movement until the lift reaches the designated height of 1.2 meters, ready for the next phase.</span></li></ul>

<h3>Secure Placement</h3>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">At the apex, the bike is slid onto the vehicle’s dedicated cradle or rail slot.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Straps equipped with tension‑release clamps fasten the frame at three points—rear axle, down tube, and front fork—distributing load evenly.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>A final visual inspection confirms that no contact points are stressed, and a digital log records the secure‑placement timestamp, reinforcing accountability for the zero‑scratch guarantee.</span></li></ul>

